{title: Angels We Have Heard on High}
{artist: Traditional French carol · tr. James Chadwick}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 96}

Verse 1
[F]Angels we have [C]heard on [F]high,
sweetly [Bb]singing [C]o'er the [F]plains,
and the mountains [C]in re[F]ply,
echo[Bb]ing their [C]joyous [F]strains.

Chorus
[F]Glo[Dm]ri[Bb]a [C]in ex[F]cel[Bb]sis [C]De[F]o,
[F]glo[Dm]ri[Bb]a [C]in ex[F]cel[Bb]sis [C]De[F]o.

Verse 2
[F]Shepherds, why this jubilee? [C]Why your joyous [F]strains
prolong? [Bb]What the [C]gladsome tidings be [F]Which
inspire your heav'nly song? [C]Gloria, in excelsis
Deo! Gloria, [C]in excelsis [F]Deo!

Verse 3
[F]Come to Bethlehem and [C]see Christ Whose [F]birth
the angels [Bb]sing; [C]Come, adore on [F]bended knee,
Christ the Lord, the newborn [C]King. Gloria, in
excelsis Deo! Gloria, [C]in [F]excelsis Deo!

Verse 4
[F]See Him in a manger [C]laid, Whom the [F]choirs of
angels praise; [Bb]Mary, [C]Joseph, lend your [F]aid, While
our hearts in love we [C]raise. Gloria, in
excelsis Deo! Gloria, [C]in [F]excelsis Deo!
